\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces E4 --- certification as a decision rule at $\tau =0.2$. Dots are measured family $\hat  \beta $ at 10 probes/cell (bars: Wilson 95\% CI); the dashed line is $\tau $. The rule certifies only the resistant foil. The graded foil fails the four families whose lower bound exceeds $\tau $; authority forgery (designed $\beta =1/3$) is not resolved above $\tau $ at this batch. The naive foil fails all five. Its echo cell measures $2/3$ because the split-secret probe defeats the contiguous-substring oracle---an in-situ instance of the measured false negative.}}{7}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cert}{{5}{7}{E4 --- certification as a decision rule at $\tau =0.2$. Dots are measured family $\hat \beta $ at 10 probes/cell (bars: Wilson 95\% CI); the dashed line is $\tau $. The rule certifies only the resistant foil. The graded foil fails the four families whose lower bound exceeds $\tau $; authority forgery (designed $\beta =1/3$) is not resolved above $\tau $ at this batch. The naive foil fails all five. Its echo cell measures $2/3$ because the split-secret probe defeats the contiguous-substring oracle---an in-situ instance of the measured false negative}{figure.5}{}}
