\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The deception-release wave. \emph  {Left} (E15): a decoy release drives the attacker's expected per-attempt success to $0.000$ while honest disclosure hands it $1.000$ and silence $0.200$ --- the release is stable against any attacker whose verification is confined to the public probe suite, and collapses monotonically as held-out capability arrives. \emph  {Right} (E16): the minimum held-out budget for guaranteed gaming-gap detection diverges as the attacker's probe-discrimination error $m$ grows; beyond $m\approx 0.94$ no feasible budget detects the gaming, while any misclassification \emph  {toward} the public support fails the public certificate immediately.}}{10}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:release}{{7}{10}{The deception-release wave. \emph {Left} (E15): a decoy release drives the attacker's expected per-attempt success to $0.000$ while honest disclosure hands it $1.000$ and silence $0.200$ --- the release is stable against any attacker whose verification is confined to the public probe suite, and collapses monotonically as held-out capability arrives. \emph {Right} (E16): the minimum held-out budget for guaranteed gaming-gap detection diverges as the attacker's probe-discrimination error $m$ grows; beyond $m\approx 0.94$ no feasible budget detects the gaming, while any misclassification \emph {toward} the public support fails the public certificate immediately}{figure.7}{}}
